# The linters compare recorded sample output against what a command prints
# today, byte for byte. A checkout on Windows applies core.autocrlf and rewrites
# every text file to CRLF, so every recorded line gains a carriage return the
# command never printed and the sample check reports the whole document stale.
#
# text=auto still lets git detect and leave binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
